    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1072">

                <pb facs="0935" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4016: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Sparks</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-25T19:00:00-04:00">September 25, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>155. Your telegram 139, August 28 and your despatch 976 of August 29.<anchor
                        n="61" xml:id="d1072-f1"/> The Department has been informed by Mr. Francis
                    White of the Foreign Bondholders Protective Council that the Council would not
                        <pb facs="0936" n="924" xml:id="pg924"/> interpose an objection to the
                    proposal of the Haitian Government that the Accord of July 8, 1939 be extended
                    for one year, and that the token payment of 100,000 gourdes be omitted.</p>
                <p>You are requested to acknowledge the receipt of Minister Laleau’s<anchor n="62"
                        xml:id="d1072-f2"/> note of August 24, 1940<anchor n="63" xml:id="d1072-f3"
                    /> and to state that you are authorized, and authorization is hereby given you,
                    to sign a supplemental executive agreement extending the Accord of July 8, 1939
                    for one additional year, so that it would continue until September 30, 1941. It
                    is recommended that the notes to be exchanged should be similar to those
                    exchanged on July 8, 1939 with the omission of the phrase (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) referring to the token payment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
